`--fail2ban` writes detections, not a line per packet. A two-party call from an
ordinary endpoint is not a detection, so the sample capture produces nothing —
this used to emit a `scanner_detected` line for the caller's INVITE, ACK and
BYE, which is every peer on a trunk handed to a tool that bans what it is given.

```
$ sipnab -N -I tests/fixtures/sip_call.pcap --fail2ban

```
